“Bespoke Health” is a secure web-based hospital management system developed to meet the needs 
of healthcare institutions like hospitals and clinics while making sure that the site is safe form 
unwanted  harm.  Built  using  Node.js,  Express,  and  PostgreSQL,  the 
architecture follows industry standards. Since the application deals with personal and medical 
records, the primary focus was on integrating security features from the ground up. This includes 
JWT-based authentication, RBAC for different user types (admin, doctor, and patient), CSRF 
protection,  input  validation,  rate  limiting,  and  secure  password  reset  mechanisms.  HTTPS  is 
enforced  using  TLS  certificates,  and  all  cookies  are  configured  with  Secure,  HttpOnly,  and 
SameSite flags to minimize the risk of session hijacking. The project also includes secure file 
uploads, audit logging, and CORS restrictions. Overall, Bespoke Health aims to provide a secure 
and reliable environment for managing hospital operations and protecting user data. 

